{"data":{"deltas":[{"range":{"end":{"character":0,"line":1},"start":{"character":0,"line":0}},"text":"Interactive Particle Collection & Obstacle Avoidance Game Extension\n\nOverview:\nThis extension transforms the static animation environment into an interactive endless-arcade survival game driven by custom Gleam DSL animations and mouse input.\n\nCore Features & Mechanics:\n1. Mouse-Driven Player Avatar: Mouse movement on the canvas maps to a player-controlled circle avatar with real-time coordinate updates handled by a Lustre message bridge.\n2. Dynamic Dual-Particle System: Evaluated Gleam code animates two distinct types of interactive shapes: positive energy nodes (reward targets) and hazardous red obstacles (bombs) that travel along parametric trajectory curves.\n3. Euclidean Collision & Health/Score Engine: On each frame tick, Euclidean distance between the cursor avatar and active particles is computed. Touching a positive node adds +10 to the score and triggers a absorption effect. Touching a hazard node deducts score/health with a screen-shake visual feedback.\n4. Endless Survival Lifecycle: The game maintains real-time Score and Health counters inside the Model, letting users test how long they can survive against increasingly dense obstacle waves defined by the animation code."}],"path":"extension.txt","source":"paste_likely"},"hash":"1debf5b87b16f966307f2cb8815adb3f6950aeae55d7ab80c435a271859ba4c1","kind":"doc.change","prev_hash":"11736b0b735709d20ea7e91ee1d8099cf68a1299a043a0c7f70fad8f0d35038e","seq":333,"t":11479808,"wall":"2026-11-11T21:36:45.074Z"}
